## Entity graph

This page turns the curated entity registry into a first-pass graph of the memoir.

The graph is intentionally simple:

- **Chapter** nodes represent memoir chapters.
- **Entity** nodes represent people, places, organizations, events, and dates.
- **MENTIONS** edges connect chapters to the entities found in them.
- **SHARES_ENTITIES_WITH** edges connect chapters that share several recurring entities.

This is not the final knowledge graph yet. It is the review layer that helps us decide which entities are important enough for the future chatbot and AWS retrieval system.

```{r}
#| echo: false
#| warning: false
#| message: false
library(readr)
library(dplyr)

nodes <- read_csv("data/public/graph_nodes.csv", show_col_types = FALSE)
edges <- read_csv("data/public/graph_edges.csv", show_col_types = FALSE)

nodes |>
  count(type, sort = TRUE, name = "node_count") |>
  knitr::kable(caption = "Graph nodes by type")
```

