## Highest-weight chapter/entity links

```{r}
#| echo: false
#| warning: false
#| message: false
edge_tbl <- read_csv("data/public/graph_edges.csv", show_col_types = FALSE)
node_tbl <- read_csv("data/public/graph_nodes.csv", show_col_types = FALSE) |>
  select(id, label, type)

edge_tbl |>
  filter(relationship == "MENTIONS") |>
  left_join(node_tbl |> rename(from_label = label, from_type = type), by = c("from" = "id")) |>
  left_join(node_tbl |> rename(to_label = label, to_type = type), by = c("to" = "id")) |>
  transmute(chapter = from_label, entity = to_label, entity_type = to_type, mentions = weight) |>
  arrange(desc(mentions), chapter, entity) |>
  head(25) |>
  knitr::kable(caption = "Top chapter-to-entity relationships")
```

## Next review questions

As you review the graph, look for these issues:

1. Are any family members duplicated under nicknames or partial names?
2. Are any places mislabeled as organizations, or organizations mislabeled as places?
3. Are broad terms like “United States” useful, or should they be down-weighted later?
4. Which entities should become first-class graph records for the future chatbot?
